\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Pareto frontier}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{multi-objective}

\p{Fix a lifecycle budget #{B}, with componentwise order on costs. The
budget-feasible outcome set is}

##{
 \mathcal V_B(M_0)
 =\left\{v\in\mathbb R^m:\exists c,\ (v,c)\in\mathfrak A(M_0),\ c\leq B\right\}.
}

\p{An outcome #{v\in\mathcal V_B(M_0)} is \strong{Pareto dominated} when
another #{v'\in\mathcal V_B(M_0)} satisfies
#{v'_j\geq v_j} for every #{j} and #{v'_k>v_k} for at least one #{k}. The
\strong{Pareto frontier} contains the attainable outcomes that are not
dominated.}

\p{Section 4.7.4 of \citef{boyd2004convex} gives the standard componentwise
Pareto order. FTIP applies that order to #{\mathcal V_B(M_0)}. The utilities,
protocol class, costs, trust conditions, and budget determine that set.}

\p{The definition preserves tradeoffs that a weighted average can hide. It
does not say which frontier point should be selected.}
